## Define Compute Image for Provisioning

The following steps import the distribution installation media for use with
xCAT. A local copy of the distribution ISO is required; for this recipe the ISO
is `{{ distro_iso_image }}`, assumed to be at `${iso_path}`.

`copycds` names the OS images after the distribution it finds inside the ISO,
including the minor release (for example a Rocky 10.0 x86_64 ISO creates
`rocky10.0-x86_64-{install,netboot,statelite}-compute`). Read that name from the
ISO, import it, and select the `{{ xcat_image_type }}` image this
{{ "stateless" if is_xcat_stateless else "stateful" }} recipe uses:

{# The image name encodes its provmethod, so the constructed name always matches
   the mode. A site that sets xcat_osimage in input.local takes responsibility for
   choosing an image whose provmethod is {{ xcat_image_type }} -- otherwise xCAT
   will provision a netboot image to local disk, or the reverse. #}

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Initialize OS images for use with xCAT -->
```bash
: "${iso_path:={{ distro_iso_image }}}"

# Read the distribution name (e.g. alma10.2) that copycds names the images after
xcat_osver=$(copycds -i "${iso_path}" | awk -F: '/^DISTNAME/{print $2}')
copycds "${iso_path}"

# Select the {{ xcat_image_type }} compute image (set xcat_osimage in input.local to override)
xcat_osimage=${xcat_osimage:-${xcat_osver}-{{ arch }}-{{ xcat_image_type }}-compute}
lsdef -t osimage -o ${xcat_osimage}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
